u.edu , Alhad Daftardar Affiliation: New York University, Brooklyn, NY, USA email: ajd9396@nyu.edu , Barath GaneshKumar Affiliation: New York University, Brooklyn, NY, USA email: bg2697@nyu.edu , Kaiyue Guo Affiliation: New York University, Brooklyn, NY, USA email: kg3209@nyu.edu , Hong Wang Affiliation: Intel, Santa Clara, CA, USA email: hong_wang@ieee.org , Benedikt Bünz Affiliation: NYU Courant, New York, NY, USA email: bb@nyu.edu , Siddharth Garg Affiliation: New York University, Brooklyn, NY, USA email: sg175@nyu.edu and Brandon Reagen Affiliation: New York University, Brooklyn, NY, USA email: bjr5@nyu.edu\nL45: ###### Abstract.\nL46: In the ZKP community, it has long been discussed that the SumCheck protocol is asymptotically more efficient than the Number Theoretic Transform (NTT), requiring only $O(N)$ arithmetic versus $O(N\\log N)$. At the same time, hardware accelerator designers propose that NTT is more hardware-friendly, benefiting from locality and data reuse, while SumCheck suffers from sequential, dependent rounds.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn3view2 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/icl-utk-edu/magma/blob/master/magmablas/gemv_batched.cu\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://github.com/icl-utk-edu/magma/blob/master/magmablas/gemv_batched.cu: Cache miss--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nmagma/COPYRIGHT at master · icl-utk-edu/magma · GitHub (https://github.com/icl-utk-edu/magma/blob/master/COPYRIGHT)\nciteturn3view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/icl-utk-edu/magma/blob/master/COPYRIGHT\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 267\nL0: 【0†Skip to content】\nL1: ## Navigation Menu\nL2: \nL3:   * Products\nL4: \nL5:     *       * 【1†GitHubRepository hosting, code review, and collaboration】\nL6:       * 【2†CopilotAI coding ag